        "name": "Maramures wooden churches and Merry Cemetery",
        "description": "Carved wooden churches, haystacks and the colourful grave crosses at Sapanta.",
        "details": "Maramures is the most traditional region, with UNESCO wooden churches such as Barsana and Surdesti, and the Merry Cemetery at Sapanta with painted crosses and funny verses. Villages have carved gates and women in traditional dress. Roads are slow.",
